From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 16:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: treat a start threshold of 0 as
 none

Userspace turns a charge limit off by writing 0 to
charge_control_start_threshold and 100 to charge_control_end_threshold
(UPower's EnableChargeThreshold(false) does this). The driver clamps the
0 up to CHARGE_CTRL_START_THR_MIN (50), so the firmware is told to
charge to 100% but resume only below 50%. A battery that stopped at the
old end threshold, say 80%, then stays at "Not charging" until it
drains below 50%, and the limit looks stuck.

Take a start threshold of 0 to mean that there is none: keep the end
threshold and use the smallest step, CHARGE_CTRL_DELTA_SOC, so charging
resumes as soon as the level drops below it. Remember the start as 0 so
that a following end threshold write keeps the small step.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c | 21 +++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -679,11 +679,27 @@
 	u32 target_soc, delta_soc;
 	int ret;
 
-	start_soc = clamp(start_soc, CHARGE_CTRL_START_THR_MIN, CHARGE_CTRL_START_THR_MAX);
-
 	mutex_lock(&battmgr->lock);
 
 	/*
+	 * A start threshold of 0 means there is none: charging resumes as soon
+	 * as the level drops below the end threshold. This is what userspace
+	 * writes to turn the limit off (start 0, end 100). Clamping it to
+	 * CHARGE_CTRL_START_THR_MIN would tell the firmware not to resume
+	 * until the battery drains below 50%, so a battery that stopped at
+	 * the old end threshold never charges to the new one. Use the
+	 * smallest step instead; a later end threshold write keeps it.
+	 */
+	if (start_soc <= 0) {
+		start_soc = 0;
+		target_soc = battmgr->info.charge_ctrl_end ?: CHARGE_CTRL_END_THR_MAX;
+		delta_soc = CHARGE_CTRL_DELTA_SOC;
+		goto set;
+	}
+
+	start_soc = clamp(start_soc, CHARGE_CTRL_START_THR_MIN, CHARGE_CTRL_START_THR_MAX);
+
+	/*
 	 * If the new start threshold is larger than the old end threshold,
 	 * move the end threshold one step (DELTA_SOC) after the new start
 	 * threshold.
@@ -698,6 +714,7 @@
 		delta_soc = battmgr->info.charge_ctrl_end - start_soc;
 	}
 
+set:
 	ret = qcom_battmgr_set_charge_control(battmgr, target_soc, delta_soc);
 	if (!ret) {
 		battmgr->info.charge_ctrl_start = start_soc;
-- 
2.53.0
